<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		Registers the reptile cold-torpor giver (built 2026-09-30).

		Why a patch and not the gene: a `GeneDef` has no field for a hediff giver, so a gene
		cannot bring one with it. Vanilla's own `OrganicStandard` set is the road every humanlike
		and every animal already walks - named in Data/Core/Defs/HediffGiverSetDefs/
		HediffGiverSets.xml and picked up by Races_Humanlike.xml, which every PMM race inherits
		from its `ParentName="Human"` - and it is where VRE registers its hypothermic hibernation
		for the same reason.

		The giver returns immediately for any pawn without the reptilian gene, so this touches
		nothing but our own mamonos: animals and vanilla humanlikes fall straight back out of it.

		Added to the list, never replacing it: the vanilla givers stay exactly as they are, and
		the torpor giver is what clears the hypothermia that still reaches a reptile.

		Fields: `hediff` is the HediffGiver base field every giver in the set uses - the hediff
		this giver builds. The rates live in C# (Source/Reptiles/ColdTorpor.cs), copied from
		vanilla's own cold numbers.
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
		<xpath>Defs/HediffGiverSetDef[defName = "OrganicStandard"]/hediffGivers</xpath>
		<value>
			<li Class="PMM_Reptiles.HediffGiver_ColdTorpor">
				<hediff>PMM_Hediff_ColdTorpor</hediff>
			</li>
		</value>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
